  "question": {
    "text": "A very long charged solid cylinder of radius 'a' contains a uniform charge density $\\rho$. Dielectric constant of the material of the cylinder is $\\mathrm{k}$. What will be the magnitude of electric field at a radial distance ' $x^{\\prime}(x    < a)$ from the axis of the cylinder?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\rho \\frac{x}{\\varepsilon_{0}}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\rho \\frac{x}{2 k \\varepsilon_{0}}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\rho \\frac{\\mathrm{x}^{2}}{2 \\mathrm{a} \\varepsilon_{0}}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\rho \\frac{\\mathrm{x}^{2}}{2 \\mathrm{k}}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint: \r\nUsing Gauss's Law\r\n$\\mathrm{E}(2 \\pi \\times \\ell)=\\frac{\\rho\\left(\\pi \\mathrm{X}^{2} \\ell\\right)}{\\mathrm{k} \\varepsilon_{0}} \\quad \\therefore \\mathrm{E}=\\frac{\\rho \\mathrm{x}}{2 \\mathrm{k} \\varepsilon_{0}}$\r\n<img src=\"assets\\st0021_89c37125a24e.png\">"
  }
}